  "final": "The suite passes now: all 7 tests are OK.\n\nThe real cause was in `reorder_qty` in `inventory/stock.py`. It computed `packs = need // pack_size`, which rounds down. The docstring and `test_reorder_rounds_up_to_whole_pack` both expect whole packs that cover the need, so it under-ordered whenever the need wasn't an exact multiple. For example, it returned 192 when 197 was needed.\n\nI changed it to round up with ceiling division: `packs = -(-need // pack_size)`.\n\nThat one test was the only failing one. Its `subTest` loop reported 183 failures, and the `[trace]` lines from the replayed streams buried them. I didn't touch the logging.",
